This paper presents a problem of knowledge recovery after machine unlearning. It is found that the unlearned model can recover the knowledge after applying quantization. The authors conduct comprehensive experiments to verify this issue and provide a theoretical analysis explaining this issue. Based on the theoretical analysis and the newly established objective, the authors propose a countermeasure to mitigate the identified issue and validate it through comprehensive and extensive experiments.

